<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<title>security.csp meta placement</title>
		<!-- The policy (script-src 'self' + hashes) doesn't allow data: URLs, so this
		     should be blocked. It runs, because Astro adds the CSP <meta> after it. -->
		<script is:inline src="data:text/javascript,window.headScriptRan=true"></script>
	</head>
	<body>
		<h1>Where Astro puts the CSP <code>&lt;meta&gt;</code></h1>
		<p>The same script, which the policy doesn't allow, in two places:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>in <code>&lt;head&gt;</code>: <strong id="head">blocked by CSP</strong> (expected: blocked by CSP)</li>
			<li>in <code>&lt;body&gt;</code>: <strong id="body">blocked by CSP</strong> (expected: blocked by CSP)</li>
		</ul>
		<script is:inline src="data:text/javascript,window.bodyScriptRan=true"></script>
		<script>
			const w = window as any;
			if (w.headScriptRan) document.getElementById('head')!.textContent = 'ran';
			if (w.bodyScriptRan) document.getElementById('body')!.textContent = 'ran';
		</script>
	</body>
</html>
